# A held zero-width rule leaves the blanks to be scanned again, so a guard
# on pre stays true: the rule would fire forever after any blank
# error: lexer_hold_keeps_pre.grammar:9:1:
# error: would match forever
# error: a held rule without a pattern sees the same whitespace again
@lexer
tokens
    gap, word, eof, err
@ pre > 0                   → gap, hold
[a-z]+                      → word
.                           → err

@parser
top! = (GAP | WORD)*        → (top ...1)
